rem Pythagorean Odds
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=285
rem Sum the expected scores of the game
rem for k up to N: a and b are random in
rem 0 to 1 and the score is k when the
rem root of (k a + 1)^2 + (k b + 1)^2
rem rounds to k, else 0

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option N integer = 100000

rem With x = k a + 1 and y = k b + 1 the
rem score is k times the share of the
rem square [1, k + 1]^2 between circles
rem of radius k - 1/2 and k + 1/2. In
rem the circle of radius R (at least the
rem root of 2) the square holds the area
rem R^2 (pi / 2 - 2 asin(1 / R)) / 2
rem - sqrt(R^2 - 1) + 1.
K = 1 to N array
Rs = concat (K + 0.5) (K - 0.5)
Rc = Rs 1.5 max
Hit = Rs * Rs at least 2
Arc = (1 / Rc) asin
Sq = Rc * Rc
Half = 1 asin
Core = Sq * (Half - 2 * Arc) / 2
Area = Core - ((Rc * Rc - 1) sqrt) + 1
Cut = Hit choose Area 0.0
Outer = Cut take N
Inner = Cut drop N
Gain = (Outer - Inner) / K
Answer = Gain sum 5 round
Answer print
